Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.99,0:00:15.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're here...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.47,0:00:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.02,0:00:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.83,0:00:22.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think the matter is?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.96,0:00:26.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once again, I'm going to have to hear the Colonel's long-winded, snide remarks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.51,0:00:29.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"You struck out on the \NPhilosopher's Stone at Liore, huh?"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.43,0:00:32.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Just how much of the military's budget \Nare you going to spend
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.07,0:00:34.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,on this fool's errand \Nbefore you're satisfied?"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.21,0:00:37.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Uh-oh, I don't see \NEdward-kun around."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.26,0:00:38.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I'm right here!"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.63,0:00:44.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Sorry, sorry, I didn't see you there \Nbehind my paperwork. Ha ha ha ha!"
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.27,0:00:51.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, like you said, we're here now, \Nso I guess I've got no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.20,0:00:52.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.55,0:00:54.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.78,0:00:58.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.30,0:01:02.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.94,0:01:06.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you up to?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.50,0:01:12.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.05,0:01:17.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.75,0:01:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.05,0:01:27.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.78,0:01:33.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.31,0:03:26.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter, Breda?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.60,0:03:28.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Havoc, watch out!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.85,0:03:30.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,O-Over there! Over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.70,0:03:35.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do we have here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.61,0:03:39.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I believe it's a dog. A carnivorous canine. \NThe scientific name is—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.07,0:03:42.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what I was asking, Warrant Officer Falman.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.24,0:03:44.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon, Lt. Hawkeye.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.68,0:03:49.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry. \NI found him this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.30,0:03:50.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Master Sgt. Fuery...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.67,0:03:52.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're keeping him?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.78,0:03:56.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wish I could, but as I'm sure you know, Lt. Havoc,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.18,0:03:57.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,animals are not permitted in the dormitories.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.88,0:04:00.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't keep him here \Nin the office because of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.49,0:04:05.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was shivering out in the rain, and I felt so sorry for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.20,0:04:06.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Will anyone else keep him?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.01,0:04:09.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm also in the dorms.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.87,0:04:13.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No way. I hate dogs.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.19,0:04:18.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, I guess I'll take him. I do like dogs, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.94,0:04:21.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much, Lieutenant!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.30,0:04:26.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear they're good \Nwhen stir-fried.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.43,0:04:29.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Out here in the eastern country, \Nthey're raised for food.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.18,0:04:31.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The redder ones in particular—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.77,0:04:34.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's look for another master.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.14,0:04:35.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.07,0:04:36.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm kidding!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.06,0:04:43.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, are you busy?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.37,0:04:47.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun, Alphonse-kun, \Nyou're back?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.95,0:04:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was that...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.68,0:04:54.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you... Al, come here!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.18,0:04:56.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun, your report!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.20,0:05:00.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll go see the Colonel directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.35,0:05:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't have capacity \Nor the conditions to keep him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.11,0:05:07.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't just go around picking up animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.61,0:05:11.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he was shivering out in the rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.63,0:05:12.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can keep him, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.83,0:05:13.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.62,0:05:15.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go drop him off \Nwhere you found him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.34,0:05:22.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, you idiot! \NYou're not human!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.38,0:05:25.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't run! \NThink about the poor cat!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.68,0:05:30.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know! I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.86,0:05:53.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds like you really did \Nquite a number on all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.31,0:05:55.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, the town of Liore?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.32,0:05:59.04,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,You're the one who gave me the information on the fake Philosopher's Stone, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.04,0:06:02.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I never told you to drive \Nthe Minister from his position.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.92,0:06:10.19,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As a result, the town has come under the rule of the Eastern Command Center, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.88,0:06:13.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, don't tell me that's what \Nyou were after in the first place!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.80,0:06:17.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that in Xenotime, the great landowner Mugear has gone missing
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.66,0:06:19.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that his mansion has collapsed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.20,0:06:24.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah? Where was this Xenotime again?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.56,0:06:27.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if I could get you to submit a report on the red water as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.07,0:06:34.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was also an inquiry from the police in the tourist resort of Aquroya.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.38,0:06:41.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it true that Psiren's \Nunmasked face is beautiful?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.56,0:06:46.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What you're trying to say is that \Nyou can tell everything we do, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.86,0:06:53.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal, why don't you try settling down already?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.30,0:06:57.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me to become one of your toadies?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.44,0:06:59.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We ourselves have a purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.92,0:07:01.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.00,0:07:04.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But it's been three years, \Nand you still haven't found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.98,0:07:10.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll find it, no matter what!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.87,0:07:22.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, do you know \Nthe name Marcoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.12,0:07:26.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a doctor and an alchemist who showed up in Xenotime five years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.85,0:07:30.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, he cured the poisoning caused by the red water,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.67,0:07:33.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,something no one else could cure, with some kind of alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.10,0:07:38.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I figured that the military would at least know the name of someone that skilled.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.47,0:07:41.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't recall it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.54,0:07:43.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I will check it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.69,0:07:46.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.15,0:08:02.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is an unexpected pleasure, Brigadier General.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.79,0:08:07.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As of today, we'll be using this office as a temporary Central Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.60,0:08:10.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A temporary Central Command Center?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.47,0:08:15.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a hassle this must be!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.74,0:08:17.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, at ease, at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.26,0:08:19.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Führer, your Excellency!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.47,0:08:25.73,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Henceforth, His Excellency the Führer, \Nand the chief command personnel under him,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.73,0:08:26.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,will be observing the Eastern Region.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.22,0:08:35.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look at all those chains!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.60,0:08:39.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those are the silver watches that \Nshow that they're State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.20,0:08:44.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means that everyone here is a State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.21,0:08:51.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, look! \NElicia can ride a tricycle now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.48,0:08:54.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She follows me around everywhere like this!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.54,0:08:58.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the same as ever, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.10,0:09:00.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've got more. Wanna see?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.71,0:09:02.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.32,0:09:06.27,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,But you know, if you're going to come see us, you could've said something ahead of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.27,0:09:10.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I wanted to see the surprised look on Mustang's face!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.00,0:09:12.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, and I'm a Lt. Colonel now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.75,0:09:15.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm in charge of investigations at the Court-Martial Office.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.53,0:09:18.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you should be in Central, shouldn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.62,0:09:20.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What can I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.51,0:09:24.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of the prominent bigwigs are \Ntrying to run away from Central—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.61,0:09:27.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean—never mind. \NEr, how have you been doing...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.93,0:09:29.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.76,0:09:32.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We might be getting closer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.94,0:09:35.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, I'm searching for \Na man named Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.97,0:09:38.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the Colonel \Nwon't tell me anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.93,0:09:41.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure he \Njust doesn't know?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.76,0:09:45.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nah, that bastard is definitely hiding something.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.94,0:09:50.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You just said "Marcoh," didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.92,0:09:52.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General Grand...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.80,0:09:55.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Iron Blood Alchemist...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.66,0:09:57.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By "Marcoh,"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.22,0:10:00.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do you mean the deserter Marcoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.54,0:10:06.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Six years ago, many State Alchemists \Nwere called up to the Eastern Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.99,0:10:10.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, Marcoh deserted the battlefield before it came to an end
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.86,0:10:12.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and has been missing ever since.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.37,0:10:15.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Deserter?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.57,0:10:19.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't know him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.64,0:10:24.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doctor Marcoh... \NDoctor Marcoh... Damn!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.14,0:10:26.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure enough, all records of him \Nhave been erased!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.93,0:10:31.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At this point, I guess I'll just have to \Nflatten the Colonel and beat it out of him!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.05,0:10:33.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Flatten him, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.78,0:10:37.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you still...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.15,0:10:40.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, you know, it hasn't stopped raining yet...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.74,0:10:43.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo! I forgot to mention \Nsomething important earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.74,0:10:44.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.54,0:10:48.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,W-Well... because of the situation,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.54,0:10:51.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this year's assessments will temporarily be held here rather than at Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.83,0:10:52.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Assessments?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.99,0:10:56.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean the assessments to renew certifications for State Alchemists?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.34,0:10:59.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll let you know later about the provisions and such—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.42,0:11:00.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hang on, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.51,0:11:02.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.59,0:11:05.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, I have a way I'd like to try handling the assessment.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.19,0:11:07.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.40,0:11:18.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Battle assessment?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.41,0:11:21.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is there such a thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.45,0:11:24.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The alchemist conducts a mock battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.16,0:11:26.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the contest itself is what gets assessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.12,0:11:30.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Edward himself \Nrequested to do this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.72,0:11:33.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what's more, he nominated the Colonel to go against?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.17,0:11:37.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, if they went at it seriously, \Nwhich one do you think is stronger?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.71,0:11:39.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That'd be the Colonel, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.82,0:11:42.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nah, you can't take \NFullmetal too lightly, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.22,0:11:47.74,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,But when you think about the stories of the Colonel's activities during the Eastern Rebellion...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.74,0:11:50.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would Edward-san propose such a thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.91,0:11:52.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that he gave the \Ncondition that if he won,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.95,0:11:56.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel would have to keep a cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.06,0:11:57.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A cat?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.67,0:12:01.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I guess we can't have \Nthe Colonel take this guy, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.05,0:12:06.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.85,0:12:10.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.90,0:12:14.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.95,0:12:16.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.18,0:12:17.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.67,0:12:19.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are loyal above all else!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.80,0:12:22.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They follow their master's orders unconditionally!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.54,0:12:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Treat them cruelly, \Nand they don't complain!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.75,0:12:26.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And they don't require a salary!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.33,0:12:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Indeed, they are servants to mankind!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.00,0:12:31.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How nice! I love dogs!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.75,0:12:37.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, Colonel, are you \Ngoing to accept Edward's challenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.02,0:12:41.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't very well go \Nall-out against a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.52,0:12:45.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It will be a shame that I cannot display my true valor.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.66,0:12:47.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.98,0:12:50.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will permit this battle assessment.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.05,0:12:51.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,B-But...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.84,0:12:54.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can use the entire parade grounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.66,0:12:57.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That way, we won't have to worry about damage to the surrounding area.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.49,0:13:00.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though you \Nweren't sure of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.72,0:13:05.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, fight the Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.52,0:13:12.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For now, I'm just going to \Ndutifully obey their words.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.69,0:13:17.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least until I achieve the rank of Führer and gain absolute power over the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.94,0:13:21.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think you might want to be more discreet about such inappropriate declarations.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.13,0:13:24.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, what could your purpose be in saying something so presumptuous?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.21,0:13:28.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a stupid question.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.23,0:13:32.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once I become Führer...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.33,0:13:39.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,all female military personnel will wear miniskirts!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.25,0:13:45.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel! I will follow you to the ends of the earth!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.24,0:13:46.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.55,0:13:49.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What pleasure!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.18,0:13:56.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ladies and gentlemen!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.76,0:13:59.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the Eastern \NCommand Center Festival!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.55,0:14:01.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And incidentally, this is...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.98,0:14:07.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,my daughter, \Nwho turned three this year!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.49,0:14:15.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elicia! Elicia!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.02,0:14:23.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And now, we'll move directly to today's main event!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.58,0:14:27.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the red corner, \Nthe Flame Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.68,0:14:29.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roy Mustang!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.43,0:14:30.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You ogre!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.35,0:14:32.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Only get yourself promoted, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.17,0:14:34.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Return my girlfriend!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.82,0:14:38.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the blue corner, \Nthe Fullmetal Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.98,0:14:40.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.81,0:14:42.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Where? Where?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.16,0:14:43.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, he's so small!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.43,0:14:45.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't see him!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.43,0:14:45.10,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Is he a grade-schooler?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.10,0:14:46.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good luck, bean sprout!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.90,0:14:50.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Small?! Don't call me small!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.02,0:14:50.91,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Calm down, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.50,0:14:54.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine, then. Today is a great day,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.88,0:14:57.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when I bust the Colonel's \Npompous mug in front of everyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.91,0:15:01.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But, Brother, \Nwe're indebted to the Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.20,0:15:05.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's overworked me, \Nsaying he'd let our secret out!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.95,0:15:07.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what's your strategy?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.00,0:15:09.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pop him with my fist!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.34,0:15:17.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The assessment doesn't matter to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.04,0:15:20.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I win, you're giving me your \Ninformation on Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.15,0:15:22.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That, and you're \Ntaking care of the cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.81,0:15:26.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.36,0:15:30.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ready...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.30,0:15:31.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.28,0:15:32.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're too slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.94,0:15:38.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give me some warning, dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.72,0:15:43.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"A soldier favors foolish haste above cleverness."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.66,0:15:47.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That means press the battle quickly, and end the battle quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.63,0:15:51.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those flames are \Nappearing out of thin air!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.81,0:15:55.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, this is the first time you've seen the Colonel do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.26,0:15:59.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His right glove is made of a special fabric, \Ncalled ignition cloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.64,0:16:02.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you rub it hard, it creates sparks.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.05,0:16:05.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All that's left is for him to adjust the density of oxygen in the air,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.28,0:16:07.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and "boom!"
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.81,0:16:15.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.66,0:16:19.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.29,0:16:24.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sure is hard to hit \Nsuch a small target!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.54,0:16:26.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't call me small!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.42,0:16:28.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"If your opponent is of choleric temper, \Nseek to irritate him."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.79,0:16:30.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't fall for the enemy's taunts.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.93,0:16:35.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've gotta be kidding!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.90,0:16:38.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Perhaps I overdid it a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.72,0:16:42.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.48,0:16:49.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.97,0:16:53.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now you can't shoot \Nany more flames!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.67,0:16:56.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're done for!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.21,0:17:22.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yow...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.77,0:17:28.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"All war is deception." Even sneak attacks make for worthy strategy, Fullmetal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.14,0:17:29.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.77,0:17:32.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You need not even ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.20,0:17:44.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's far enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.25,0:17:47.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a magnificent fight!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.78,0:17:50.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We are honored by \Nyour words of praise!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.32,0:17:52.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on! \NWe're not through yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.93,0:17:55.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm, \Nbut if you go any further,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.55,0:17:59.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it will be tougher to \Ntidy up afterward, won't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.91,0:18:11.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They've got no choice. Both of them were ordered to fix everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.53,0:18:18.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is why I didn't want to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.49,0:18:21.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, why did you hold back?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.62,0:18:25.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your last shot—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.52,0:18:27.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you should've had the timing for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.79,0:18:35.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This goes back many years now,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.93,0:18:38.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there was something \Ncalled the Ishbalan Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.40,0:18:42.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the east, when the Ishbalans clashed with the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.87,0:18:48.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw... many unpleasant things...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.70,0:19:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doctor Marcoh, \Nwho deserted the battlefield,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.47,0:19:24.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,was the most sensible man among us. \NI still think so, even now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.06,0:19:28.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that why you kept quiet about him?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.00,0:19:33.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, perhaps you ought to see Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.67,0:19:34.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's alive?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.30,0:19:44.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, I still haven't heard the reason why you stopped on that last shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.88,0:19:47.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nah,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.53,0:19:49.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.09,0:19:54.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If there are no other \Ncandidates to keep him,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.83,0:19:57.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will take him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.52,0:19:58.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.22,0:20:07.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, now, just because you're relieved...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.42,0:20:20.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My discipline is strict.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.94,0:20:25.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on now, the bathroom is over here. \NGot that, Black Hayate?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.84,0:20:28.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Black Hayate?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.17,0:20:33.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About the town of Liore, \Nin Ed's report...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.81,0:20:37.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you know that General Hakuro's detachment had been dispatched there?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.47,0:20:40.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear there's a terrible \Ncivil war going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.78,0:20:43.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed wrote that the Minister had fallen,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.68,0:20:46.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that the people would likely open their eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.46,0:20:48.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Minister is doing fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.09,0:20:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I understand he's inciting the citizens to wage war against the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.35,0:20:56.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't be sure whether or not it's the same minister that Ed defeated, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.30,0:20:59.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you going to send Ed in again to investigate?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.92,0:21:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He believes he's saved a town.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.90,0:21:06.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can let him believe that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.18,0:21:09.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He'll find out on his own sometime.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.98,0:21:15.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've gotten the information on Marcoh from the Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.20,0:21:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't very well ask him to take care of this too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.22,0:21:20.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It would go against the \NPrinciple of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.86,0:21:22.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, it would.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.98,0:21:29.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, but right now, \Nthis is all we can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.54,0:21:41.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't it about time you told me?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.27,0:21:44.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not here to observe us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.40,0:21:49.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bigwigs conned the Führer \Ninto fleeing here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.79,0:21:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In Central alone, there are already five State Alchemists and staff
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.70,0:21:56.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who have been killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.04,0:22:21.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,East City...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.49,0:23:40.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.28,0:23:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 14: "Destruction's Right Hand"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.65,0:23:47.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if all of the State Alchemists are your enemies,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.71,0:23:50.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't allow you to kill Brother!
